.\" Title: vrw-cert-show
.\" Author: vrw contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\" Process this file with
.\"   groff -man -Tascii vrw-cert-show.1

.TH VRW\-CERT\-SHOW 1 "2025" "vrw" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrw\-cert\-show \- display full details of a certificate including its bearer token

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrw
\fBcert show\fR \fINAME\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
Display full details of a specific certificate in the vrw certificate pool, including the complete 64-character bearer token. This token is required for API authentication when accessing certificate-bound commands.

The bearer token is displayed in two forms: the full 64-character SHA-256 hex string, and a truncated 16-character preview (same as shown by \fBcert list\fR). The full token should be kept confidential and used in the \fBAuthorization: Bearer <token>\fR HTTP header when making API requests.

This subcommand is synchronous and does not require a running vrw instance. It reads the certificate PEM file from disk and computes the derived token.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B NAME
Name of the certificate to display (as given to \fBcert generate\fR).

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Show full certificate details:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw cert show my-app\fR
Certificate: my-app
  Certificate: /home/user/.config/vrw/certs/my-app/cert.pem
  Key:        /home/user/.config/vrw/certs/my-app/key.pem
  Token:      a3f8c1e2b7d94001b8c3d2e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b6
  Token (16): a3f8c1e2b7d94001...
.fi
.RE

.PP
Use the token in a curl request:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ TOKEN=$(vrw cert show my-app | grep "Token:" | head -1 | awk '{print $2}')\fR
\fB$ curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \e\fR
     http://localhost:9090/api/commands
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Certificate details displayed successfully.

.TP
.B 1
Error (certificate not found, file read error, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR vrw\-cert (1),
.BR vrw\-cert\-generate (1),
.BR vrw\-cert\-list (1),
.BR vrw\-cert\-remove (1),
.BR vrw (1)
